# Teval's "you lose life equal to its mana value" reads the spell as it last existed on the stack when it has left (CR 608.2h),
# its X counted as chosen (CR 202.3e; ruling 2025-04-04). Bot1 casts Walking Ballista for X = 2 ({4}: three Moxen and one
# Lotus Petal exiled to delve), and Bot2 counters it in response to Teval's trigger. The trigger still resolves: Bot1 loses 4,
# not the 0 the Ballista card has in the graveyard. Bot2's Counterspell is not Bot1's spell, so Bot1 loses nothing for it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Teval, Arbiter of Virtue
Lotus Petal
Lotus Petal
Walking Ballista
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Counterspell
Island x20

